<title>USA: Chile buys 1.3 mln bbls of Forcados, Oriente crude.</title>
<headline>Chile buys 1.3 mln bbls of Forcados, Oriente crude.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's state oil company, Empresa Nacional del Petroleo (ENAP), bought 950,000 barrels of Forcados crude and 360,000 barrels of Oriente for delivery April 10-14, trade sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>ENAP bought both cargoes from Swiss-based trader Glencore.</p>
<p>The Ecuadoran Oriente was sold at an undisclosed price based on West Texas Intermediate/Cushing.</p>
<p>In last week's crude tender, however, ENAP paid a discount of $3.50-4.00 to May WTI for the same size cargo of Oriente.</p>
<p>The Nigerian Forcados was sold on a dated-related basis.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
